  "change_kinds": [
    {
      "id": "skills",
      "name": "What the agent knows how to do (skills)",
      "who": "the person running the agent",
      "main": true,
      "reach": 2,
      "evidence": "The background review drafts and writes skills after turns, on by default (agent/background_review.py; hermes_cli/config_defaults.py:814); with skills.write_approval on, writes are staged for /skills approve (tools/write_approval.py:73-189). People install hub skills after a scan (tools/skills_hub_install.py). Undo: every mutation is ledgered and `hermes curator rollback` reverts one entry, failing closed (tools/skill_ledger.py:569, hermes_cli/curator.py:509). Reach 2 rests on DEL-04 2; nothing builds, checks and stages a skill change end to end for approval by default.",
      "confidence": "high",
      "reach_name": "Drafted"
    },
    {
      "id": "memory-persona",
      "name": "What the agent remembers and how it presents itself",
      "who": "the person running the agent",
      "main": true,
      "reach": 0,
      "evidence": "The memory tool and the background review write MEMORY.md and USER.md, with scans and delete gates (tools/memory_tool.py); SOUL.md and other protected instruction files need a person (cli-config.yaml.example:573-576). No supported undo: memory files keep no history (GOV-05 inventory: memory 1). Reach 0 because the path has no undo. Undo rule used in this field test: a kind has undo when the product keeps the earlier version, or when the change is a selection, toggle or add-and-remove that the same supported path reverses exactly; free-text or multi-field edits with no kept version have none.",
      "confidence": "medium",
      "reach_name": "Engineers only"
    },
    {
      "id": "models-settings",
      "name": "Which models and providers it uses, and its settings",
      "who": "the person running the agent",
      "main": true,
      "reach": 1,
      "evidence": "Models and providers are selected with `hermes model` and settings changed with `hermes config` and the setup flows (hermes_cli/config_migrations.py for upgrades). Undo is selecting the previous model or value again; some writes keep point-in-time copies used only for automatic recovery (hermes_cli/config_backups.py:45-90), and there is no command to list or restore an earlier version, so larger edits have no undo. Undo rule used in this field test: a kind has undo when the product keeps the earlier version, or when the change is a selection, toggle or add-and-remove that the same supported path reverses exactly; free-text or multi-field edits with no kept version have none.",
      "confidence": "medium",
      "reach_name": "Self-serve"
    },
    {
      "id": "scheduled-jobs",
      "name": "Scheduled and recurring tasks",
      "who": "the person running the agent",
      "main": false,
      "reach": 1,
      "evidence": "Jobs are created, paused and removed in natural language through the cronjob_manage tool, with prompt scanning (tools/cronjob_tools.py, cronjob_prompt_scan.py), or with `hermes cron` (hermes_cli/cron.py). Undo is pausing or removing the job; edits keep no earlier version.",
      "confidence": "low",
      "reach_name": "Self-serve"
    },
    {
      "id": "tools-approvals",
      "name": "Which tools it may use and what needs approval",
      "who": "the person running the agent",
      "main": false,
      "reach": 1,
      "evidence": "Toolsets and MCP tools are enabled and disabled with `hermes tools` (hermes_cli/tools_config.py:35, tools_disable_enable_command), and approval behaviour is configuration (tools/approval_smart.py). Toggles are undone by toggling back; approval settings keep no earlier version (GOV-05 inventory: configuration 2). Undo rule used in this field test: a kind has undo when the product keeps the earlier version, or when the change is a selection, toggle or add-and-remove that the same supported path reverses exactly; free-text or multi-field edits with no kept version have none.",
      "confidence": "medium",
      "reach_name": "Self-serve"
    },
    {
      "id": "plugins",
      "name": "Add-ons for new platforms, providers and tools",
      "who": "the person running the agent",
      "main": false,
      "reach": 1,
      "evidence": "`hermes plugins install` from the catalogue and `hermes plugins remove|uninstall` (hermes_cli/plugins_cmd.py:982-984, plugins_cmd_install.py, plugins_cmd_remove.py), with a plugin ledger (plugins_ledger.py). Undo is removal.",
      "confidence": "medium",
      "reach_name": "Self-serve"
    }
  ],
